<title>SWITZERLAND: Canada says improving offer in telecom talks.</title>
<headline>Canada says improving offer in telecom talks.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada is submitting an improved offer in global talks on a world pact to liberalise basic telecommunications, a Canadian negotiating official said.</p>
<p>The official, who asked not to be named, said the offer would deal with access and use of satellite services and not foreign ownership of telecom companies.</p>
<p>&quot;A good package is taking shape in the talks, and this has encouraged us to make an extra effort to try to get an agreement finalised,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The negotiations face a midnight (2300GMT) deadline on February 15 for completion.</p>
<p>Geneva Newsroom --  41 22 733 38 31</p>
